#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:ConfidenceAsProbabilityConstraint (Rule P10): a
# math:ProbabilityValue that carries a logic:confidence AND declares the logic:probabilityModel
# that licenses reading that confidence as a probability, so the confidence→probability
# SHACL-SPARQL gate stays silent. The declared model also satisfies the framing gate
# math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (P3, via the probabilityModel arm of its sh:or). It is
# not typed math:OddsValue / math:LogOddsValue (P2). It MUST raise NO probability failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/confidence-as-probability.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConfidenceWithModel).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:calibratedProbability a math:ProbabilityValue ;
    logic:confidence "0.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
    logic:probabilityModel ex:logisticCalibrationModel .

ex:logisticCalibrationModel a math:MathematicalObject .
<http://example.org/math/calibratedProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
